# Build context for `services/api/Dockerfile`, whose context is this directory
# (see the header there). Two jobs:
#
#   1. keep the context small — a full `node_modules` plus `apps/mobile/android`
#      is well over a gigabyte and none of it is used by the image;
#   2. keep secrets out of the context ENTIRELY, so no future `COPY` can put one
#      in a layer even by accident. `.env` and the release keystore are the two
#      that would matter, and losing the keystore is unrecoverable
#      (apps/mobile/keystores/README.md).

# Never in an image. Secrets reach the box through infra/push-secrets.sh.
.env
.env.*
*.keystore
*.jks
apps/mobile/keystores/
credentials.json

# STATE_DIR — live wallet and agent ids from whoever ran this checkout.
.state/

node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
build/
**/build/
*.tsbuildinfo

.git/
.github/
.claude/
.worktrees/

# Nothing the API image needs.
apps/
services/indexer/
infra/
docs/
*.md
*.log
